ars on the cover of issue 29 of the  comic book Dazzler  and there's another amusing moment in  the record store when Scott picks up an  album featuring Boy George and ask Jean  has anyone ever told you you look like  this  although Jubilees role was cut down in  the final film they did shoot an  important scene at the shopping mall  where she got to use her powers in the  comics Jubilee has the power to produce  explosive balls of energy plasma or  fireworks by the way the shopping mall  itself is an easter egg - how jubilee  discovered her powers in the comics  after running away from a mall security  guard and it's also where she met at the  x-men members including storm rogue  psylocke and Dazzler it's actually  rumored that the deleted scene is  similar to the comics with Jubilee using  her powers and then having to escape  from the mole security using her  gymnastic abilities Nightcrawler  also had some funny scenes at the mall  including a moment where he started  break dancing with a group of kids and  in another funny scene the four mutants  are drinking cold drinks when  Nightcrawler becomes scared as he got an  ice-cream headache but when Scott tells  him not to worry is just a brain freeze  Nightcrawler gets even more frightened  as he thinks his brain is about to  freeze over also hidden in the mole  sequences in a marsh in the 1980s movie  Moscow on the Hudson starring Robin  Williams as the young mutants walk  around Nightcrawler who is new to  America is amazed that ordinary people  don't fear than was mutants Nightcrawler  thinks the mall is a paradise and it  parallels how Robin Williams Russian  character feels when he arrives in  America in the movie Moscow on the  Hudson in the film Williams plays a  Soviet musician in the circus who  defects during a visit to Bloomingdale's  in New York which is doubly interesting  as Nightcrawler  also performed in the circus before he  met the x-men prior to Scotts mantra he  was at the x-mansion with his brother  Alex aka havoc and just before Alex left  was Charles to visit Moira at the CIA  the on-screen brothers filmed a farewell  scene this would have been the last  moment Cyclops shared with his brother  havoc as it was while Cyclops is  returning from the malls that havoc died  during the x-mansion explosion  Bryan Singer has mentioned that Michael  Fassbender filmed a beautiful scene  outdoors which brought tears to the  filmmakers eyes from what singer has  said it sounds like the scene was of  magneto with his polish family  according to singer although the scene  was incredible it just didn't fit in the  overall story in the movie apocalypse  has four horsemen storm Angel Psylocke  and magneto was in an earlier version of  the script apocalypse only had storm  angel and magneto as his three horsemen  and there were no plans at all to  include Psylocke in the movie the  initial script had Charles being  kidnapped by apocalypse with the  intention of counting him as the fourth  Horseman but Kinberg and singer realized  that this wouldn't really work so they  looked through the comic book history of  the various horsemen and thought that  Psylocke was the most intriguing the  filmmakers had actually just met with  Olivia Munn to talk about a pot in  Deadpool and it was when they came  across some fanart of her ass I locked  that they thought she'd be perfect for  the role Olivia Munn's role in the movie  changed again even after she was cast  initially it was announced that she'll  be playing Betsy Braddock who in her  comic book origins story grows up in the  UK Olivia Munn is a huge fan of psylocke  and the characters comic book history  however the filmmakers decided that the  movie with not explore Betsy's life  before she became psylocke for example  her time as a pilot or a model and she  wouldn't have a British accent either  Wolverines cameo could have turned out  quite differently and there were many  versions that were considered including  not having 